  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Npc191948 and the High-affinity choline transporter, mediated through a series of targets. Npc191948 is implicated in the regulation of 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including 24-Methylenecycloartanone and (+)-(5S,7R)-7-Ethoxy-12-Hydroxy-2-Oxo-20-Norabieta-1(10),8,11,13-Tetraene. These compounds are all predicted to interact with the High-affinity choline transporter, indicating a possible pathway through which Npc191948 may influence the transporter's activity. The scores from the models suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The evidence highlights a potential regulatory network involving proteasomal subunits and choline transporter modulation, underscoring the complexity of the biological processes involved.",
